AI can be used to help with various tasks. A junior can use it to assist with analysis and observing and alerting possible anomalies that an analyst may miss due to alert fatigue. AI can assist by handling repetitive tasks, accelerating research, enhancing predictive modelling, and real-time anomaly detection.

Human intervention can still be kept priority by:
  •	Allowing people to validate the final decision and applying business intuition, context and client-specific understanding that algorithms lack. 
  •	Analysts can cross-check the validity of AI to minimise the possibility of hallucinations. 
  •	Analysts must also ensure sensitive information is not fed to AI and not risk the possibility of sensitive data loss

The integration of AI into data and financial analysis can be pivotal to the rate of result production and risk mitigation. Using AI to analyse and cross-reference data to ensure validity and integrity based on other internet resources can maintain data validity and that all processes follow due protocol. This can increase organisation credibility while contributing to technological innovation.
